      "content": "i mean, i get the nervousness thing, but it didn't just look like twitchy muscles. it looked like the movement itself was slightly... asynchronous. almost like the facial mapping didn't quite catch up to the audio. if you look closely at the way the skin around the eyes moved compared to the cheek, it felt less like a biological reflex and more like a digital overlay or something. you don't think it's possible that what we're seeing is actually some kind of high-end deepfake or a replacement being used for public appearances? it's getting harder to tell the difference lately.",
